<title>INDIA: Bank Internasional Indonesia cuts India prime rate.</title>
<headline>Bank Internasional Indonesia cuts India prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Internasional Indonesia said on Thursday it had cut its Indian prime lending rate to 16.5 percent per annum from 17.5 percent, effective April 17.</p>
<p>The spread over the prime lending rate is four percentage points, a bank official said.</p>
<p>The bank's cut in interest rate follows reductions announced by a number of other banks after the Reserve Bank of India released its credit and monetary policy for first half 1997/98 (April-March) on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
